  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.046,
            0.861,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proportional Reasoning-1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The second term should also change by the same factor. When 10 increases by a factor of 3, it becomes 30. Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.425,
            0.13,
            0.573,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6 : 10 :: 18 : 30."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.154,
            0.847,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, she should use 30 spoons of sugar to make 18 glasses of lemonade with the same sweetness as earlier."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.203,
            0.848,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Nitin and Hari were constructing a compound wall around their house. Nitin was building the longer side, 60 ft in length, and Hari was building the shorter side, 40 ft in length. Nitin used 3 bags of cement but Hari used only 2 bags of cement. Nitin was worried that the wall Hari built would not be as strong as the wall he built because she used less cement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.311,
            0.459,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is Nitin correct in his thinking?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.337,
            0.847,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Nitin and Hari’s case, we should compare the ratio of the length of the wall to the bags of cement used by each of them and see whether they are proportional."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.395,
            0.768,
            0.414
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The ratio in Nitin’s case is 60 : 3, i.e., 20 : 1 (in its simplest form)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.413,
            0.764,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The ratio in Hari’s case is 40 : 2, i.e., 20 : 1 (in its simplest form)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.432,
            0.846,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since both ratios are proportional, the walls are equally strong. Nitin should not worry!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.48,
            0.847,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In my school, there are 5 teachers and 170 students. The ratio of teachers to students in my school is 5 : 170. Count the number of teachers and students in your school. What is the ratio of teachers to students in your school? Write it below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.593,
            0.847,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？my school?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.648,
            0.848,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 5:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Measure the width and height (to the nearest cm) of the blackboard in your classroom. What is the ratio of width to height of the blackboard?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.736,
            0.846,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you draw a rectangle in your notebook whose width and height are proportional to the ratio of the blackboard?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.784,
            0.8,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Compare the rectangle you have drawn to those drawn by your classmates. Do they all look the same?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.771,
            0.904,
